---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ResourceLibrary from '../components/ResourceLibrary';
---
<Layout title="Resources — PRINCE">
  <section class="page-hero wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Prince</a><span>/</span><span>Resources</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Open the notebook</span><h1>The work,<br /><em>within reach.</em></h1><p class="lede">The model, the protocol, the comparisons, and the uncertainty. Ten curated artifacts, ready to inspect.</p></section>
  <div class="wrap"><section class="content-section"><ResourceLibrary client:load /><noscript><p>JavaScript is needed to filter the library. All artifacts remain available: <a href="/prince/model-evaluation.json">model evaluation</a>, <a href="/prince/site-evaluation.json">site evaluation</a>, <a href="/prince/site-uncertainty.json">uncertainty</a>, <a href="/prince/fit-protocol.json">fit protocol</a>, <a href="/prince/connected-manifest.csv">manifest</a>, <a href="/prince/antigen-context-audit.json">antigen audit</a>, <a href="/prince/bepipred-comparison.json">comparison</a>, <a href="/prince/bepipred-inference-provenance.json">inference provenance</a>, <a href="/prince/bepipred-verification.json">verification</a>, <a href="/prince/LICENSE.txt">license</a>.</p></noscript></section>
  <section class="content-section" id="demo"><div class="two-column"><div><span class="eyebrow">A real run, recorded</span><h2>See the engine<br /><em>at work.</em></h2></div><div><p>This recording shows the working analysis in the original PRINCE interface supplied with the handoff. The website has a new design; the underlying analysis, source provenance, and review gates are carried forward.</p><p class="research-note">Original-interface demonstration · 76.68 seconds · 1440 × 1000</p></div></div><video class="demo-player" controls preload="metadata" playsinline aria-label="Recorded original PRINCE interface demonstration"><source src="/media/prince-live-demo.webm" type="video/webm" /><a href="/media/prince-live-demo.webm">Download the demonstration</a></video><p class="research-note">This recording is a historical demonstration, not the output of a new analysis. Use the workspace to run your own target.</p></section>
  <section class="content-section two-column"><div><span class="eyebrow">Read, reuse, attribute</span><h2>Open code.<br /><em>Specific licenses.</em></h2><p>PRINCE is MIT licensed. That license does not relicense dependencies, structural data, source publications, or BepiPred. Their own terms continue to apply.</p><a class="text-link" href="/prince/LICENSE.txt">Read the PRINCE license <span>↗</span></a></div><div><h3>Keep provenance with the result.</h3><p>When reporting or reusing the supplied evaluation, preserve its frozen model and source hashes, split definitions, denominators, and retrospective limitations.</p><p>The downloadable collection is the curated public surface of the handoff. Full scientific regeneration also needs the original coordinate and metadata caches, and external comparator weights where applicable.</p></div></section><div class="inline-cta"><h2>Ready to <em>look closer?</em></h2><a class="button" href="/workspace/">Explore your target <span>↗</span></a></div></div>
</Layout>
